  - Cannot distinguish std::stoi-with-try/catch from strtol+errno/range-check or a hand-rolled strtol-equivalent with an explicit i32 range check: all three agree on every input tested, including the 2^32+80 discriminator. The observable grammar and range are identical, so any of them is a faithful reproduction.
  - A 0x00 byte inside the port substring cannot be tested via argv.

